thread:
Sara (Sales): team, new pilot inbound — Northwell wants a 2-week POC: Go SDK, streaming responses, function/tool calls to their inventory service, and strictly validated JSON output. EU residency. Can we support?
Jonah (Presales): yes on paper. main concerns: deterministic schema (no extra prose), streaming so UI can show partial results, and toolcall reliability. they asked about sample schema enforcement and SDK retries.
Lina (SRE): infra note: Dedicated in eu-west recommended for residency + predictable latency. For sustained 180 qps we need reserved units; enable burst pool for spikes to ~900 qps. provisioning estimate: 3 business days for sandbox.
Omar (Security): security checklist: BYOK, audit logs, SSO (SAML), encryption in transit+rest, and pen-test window. we need completed security questionnaire before prod. share SOC2 artifacts.
Jonah (Presales): can we show a minimal Go streaming example that demonstrates partial toolcall events and schema enforcement? customer engineers prefer code.
PlatformBot: here's a compact Go sketch (streaming + function call detection):
```go
// pseudo-code - use redwood-go-sdk vX.Y
ctx := context.Background()
req := &redwood.Request{
  Model: "rwd-std-1",
  Stream: true,
  ResponseSchema: map[string]interface{}{
    "type":"object",
    "properties": map[string]interface{}{
      "action": map[string]interface{}{"type":"string"},
      "payload": map[string]interface{}{"type":"object"},
    },
    "required": []string{"action","payload"},
    "enforce": true,
  },
}
err := client.Stream(ctx, req, func(evt redwood.Event){
  switch evt.Type {
  case redwood.EventToken:
    // show partial tokens in UI
  case redwood.EventFunctionCall:
    // accumulate args until evt.FunctionComplete == true
    // then call their inventory API with timeout/context
  case redwood.EventDone:
    // final validation passed by runtime (enforce=true)
  }
})
if err != nil { log.Fatal(err) }
```
Jonah (Presales): also include a JSON schema example the customer can paste into their parser: 
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "action": {"type":"string"},
    "payload": {"type":"object", "properties": {"sku": {"type":"string"}, "qty": {"type":"integer"}}}
  },
  "required": ["action","payload"]
}
```
Lina (SRE): runtime enforcement with "enforce":true will drop nonconforming tokens and return schema error events. still recommend app-side guard rails: small stateful validator to avoid retries on transient schema errors. set external call timeout 1.5s and circuit-breaker.
Omar (Security): for BYOK note: Private deployment with customer KMS integration supported. HSM optional. must confirm key rotation cadence and backup retention. sec questionnaire link: https://redwood.internal/sec/presales-questionnaire (fill and attach).
Sara (Sales): pricing ask from Northwell: what is a ballpark for 2-week POC (dedicated sandbox + burst)?
Lina (SRE): rough sketch: sandbox reserved capacity for 180 qps ~ $8.5k/mo pro-rata for 2 weeks -> ~$2.1k; burst addon ~+25% for trial. engineering support hours for onboarding ~8-12 hrs (SE time). note this is sketch, finance to confirm.
Jonah (Presales): success criteria to propose: 1) p95 latency < 300ms for <256 token responses, 2) zero schema violations for 95% of calls, 3) successful toolcall integrations with <1% failure rate.
Sara (Sales): Northwell requested an ops runbook + rollback plan. what should we include?
Lina (SRE): runbook bullets:
- onboarding checklist (IP ranges, SAML metadata, KMS ARN),
- traffic ramp steps (10% -> 50% -> 100%),
- observability (token cost, per-route latency, schema-violation alerts),
- fallback policy: route to quantized variant or degrade streaming -> non-streaming,
- emergency rollback: disable route, drain connections, revert to previous model image.
Omar (Security): add: incident reporting flow, data export request process, retention policy, and pen-test scheduling window.
Jonah (Presales): action items:
- Sara: collect Northwell IP ranges, SAML metadata, and POC technical contact (due EOD).
- Lina: start sandbox provisioning once Sara supplies contact (ETA 3 biz days).
- Omar: send SOC2 artifacts + presales questionnaire link to customer.
- Jonah: prepare Go SDK sample repo and a short demo script.
Sara (Sales): pinged Northwell for info. demo slot requested Wed 11:00 CET. I'll update thread when they confirm.
PlatformBot: reminder set: follow up in 48h for security checklist completion.
